<Project>
  <!--
    Host-side scale arithmetic, shared by SOURCE rather than as a package or a project reference.

    Same reasoning as WebCore.props one directory over, for a smaller unit. HostScale is the
    logical/device/effective-scale model every windowed host needs (#137) and it is pure managed
    arithmetic with no dependencies at all — not the engine, not a windowing library.

    Compiled in rather than referenced for three reasons:

      * The ENGINE stays exactly as it is. src/CupriFace has zero P/Invoke and no host concepts in
        it, and a scale model that only hosts use is not a reason to start.
      * It never enters the browser hosts' ILC input. CupriFace.Web.NativeAot compiles the whole
        program when the app publishes; a type that is not in the compile cannot cost a wasm byte,
        which is a stronger guarantee than trusting the trimmer to remove it.
      * The TESTS can reach it without a CupriFace.Shell reference, which would pull Silk.NET and
        SDL into every unit-test run for the sake of arithmetic that needs no window.

    Nothing here crosses an assembly boundary: hosts consume HostScale and hand the engine plain
    floats, so the type being compiled into more than one assembly is invisible — the same property
    WebCore.props already relies on.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)CupriFace.Hosting\*.cs" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
